{{also|Tyo|tyó}}
==Finnish==

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|fi|work}}
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*töö|id=work}} (compare {{cog|et|töö}}, {{cog|liv|tīe}}, {{cog|vot|töö}}), from {{inh|fi|fiu-pro|*tewe}} (compare {{cog|myv|тев}}).

====Noun====
{{fi-noun}}

# [[work]] {{gloss|labour, employment, occupation, job}}
# [[work]] {{gloss|effort expended on a particular task}}
# [[work]] {{gloss|place of work}} {{q|locative cases in the plural}}
#: {{syn|fi|työpaikka|duuni<q:slang>}}
# [[job]] {{gloss|economic role for which a person is paid}}
#: {{syn|fi|duuni<q:slang>}}
# [[work]] {{gloss|artistic or intellectual production}}
#: {{syn|fi|teos}}
# {{lb|fi|physics|mechanics|thermodynamics}} [[work]] {{gloss|measure of energy}}

=====Usage notes=====
* When saying "at work", "to work" or "from work", the locational cases are used in the plural:
*: {{uxi|fi|Olen '''töissä'''.|I am at '''work'''.}}
*: {{coi|fi|mennä '''töihin'''|to go to '''work'''}}

